    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0203" n="194" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg194"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115 European War 1939/277: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-02-19T23:00:00+00:00">February 19,
                            1940—11 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 19—6:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>420. Berlin’s 438, February 17, 2 p.m.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d260-f1"/> Does the
                    Department wish me to make any specific observations in communicating the
                    substance of Berlin’s telegram under reference to the British Foreign Office?
                        <pb facs="0204" n="195" xml:id="pg195"/> I believe that it should be
                    communicated to the Foreign Office without delay.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
